The UI spec §6 says: 'Contrast of text against both background and surface below 4.5:1 is logged as a warning, not refused' - the wording 'against both' came with k17 itself (0f7e21f). The resolver computes contrast once, against CANLIN_THEME_BACKGROUND only (src/ui/theme.c:250); CANLIN_THEME_SURFACE appears in no contrast call in the tree. Panels are drawn on the surface (src/ui/ui.c:2425 fills with CANLIN_THEME_SURFACE, src/ui/theme.c:309 maps it into the style table), so text on a panel can be unreadable while the resolver stays silent. A probe against the shipped theme.o with text=#767676, background=#ffffff (4.54:1) and surface=#8a8a8a (1.32:1) logs nothing. t/ui/test_theme.c:373-395 exercises only the background pair. The header at include/canlin/theme.h:96 states the narrower rule, so code and header agree with each other and disagree with the spec. Found by the 2026-11-14 review of k17.

Resolver now warns for both pairs (text/background and text/surface), each line naming its pair; the theme is still never refused. Header contract in include/canlin/theme.h now states the rule the code implements. Test first: t/ui/test_theme.c test_contrast failed with 3 assertions (only the background pair was checked), then green. Host suite green (make test: ALL TESTS PASSED, theme: all passed).

Done: canlin_theme_resolve warns once per pair below 4.5:1 (text/background, text/surface), each line naming the pair; still a warning, never a refusal (UI spec §6). New helper warn_contrast() in src/ui/theme.c; header contract include/canlin/theme.h:96 updated. Regression test in t/ui/test_theme.c (test_contrast): red first (3 failed assertions), green after the fix. Host: make + make test green, ./build/host/t/ui/test_theme passes. Finding for the board: nk_init_default() in the vendored Nuklear always returns 1 (third_party/nuklear/nuklear.h:19658), so the ENOMEM path of canlin_ui_view_new is unreachable today - see k92.

